     1,
     "<div>Hi YA, </div><div><br></div><div>Sorry, I’m not entirely sure what you mean by the &quot;starting point,&quot; but typically, the initial value of a parameter estimate is set randomly within the specified range for each parameter. This approach helps minimize the potential bias from the initial values on the parameter estimation. I hope this clarifies things, and please feel free to reach out if anything is unclear!<br><br></div><div>Best, </div><div>JH </div>"
    ],
